course: dictionary
lesson: 7117
title: Peel: a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Peel» can be a verb (an action word) or a noun (a naming word). As a verb it means to take the skin off something, or to come off by itself. As a noun it is the skin itself. Context tells you which: «Peel the potatoes» is an action, while «put the banana peel in the bin» names a thing.
explain: «If a blister bursts, leave the loose skin in place and cover it, rather than peeling it off.» Here peeling it off means pulling the skin away. The words leave and cover tell you that is the thing not to do. Always ask: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: «Take those ridiculous things off!» «Shan't!» So the Rat sits on him and the Mole peels his motor-clothes off bit by bit. Peels off here means takes off slowly, one layer at a time. In stories, «Keep your eyes peeled» has nothing to do with skin: it means watch carefully.
fact: Peel can be a verb (peel, peels, peeled, peeling) or a noun (peel).
fact: To peel means to take the skin off fruit or vegetables.
fact: The peel is the skin, like a banana peel or orange peel.
fact: Peel can also mean a thin layer comes off by itself, as in paint peels or skin peels after sunburn.
fact: «Keep your eyes peeled» means watch carefully.
exercise: «Take those ridiculous things off!» «Shan't!» So the Rat sits on him and the Mole peels his motor-clothes off bit by bit. What does peels mean here? | Paints them | *Takes them off slowly, one layer at a time | Hangs them up to dry | Washes them clean
exercise: «If a blister bursts, leave the loose skin in place and cover it, rather than peeling it off.» What should you do with loose skin on a blister? | *Leave it in place and cover it | Rub it with a cloth | Pull it off quickly | Peel it off to see what is under it
exercise: «Along the way fibre from apple peel keeps things moving.» Find and copy the word that names the skin of an apple. | *peel | fibre | things | apple
test: «Keep your eyes peeled» means: | Cry a little | Look away from the road | *Watch carefully | Close your eyes tightly
test: «Old paint peels in the sun and rain.» What does peels mean here? | Is washed clean | Shines brightly | Is painted over quickly | *Comes off in thin layers by itself
exam: In «The peel is in the bin, and Sam peeled the apple», which word is a verb? | The | apple | bin | *peeled
